1
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:32,450
Now, hurry up and drop your weapon.

2
00:01:35,990 --> 00:01:38,170
Step back and get on your hands and knees.

3
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:40,570
You move even one bit and I'll kill her.

4
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:44,890
Hey, Laios, she was one of Shuro's followers, wasn't she?

5
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:48,190
Oh, yeah, then she was tailing us this whole time.

6
00:01:48,610 --> 00:01:51,090
You! Get the spell off me!

7
00:01:51,490 --> 00:01:51,750
Huh?

8
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:54,990
The spell that's been cast on me! Hurry up and get rid of it!

9
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:57,970
Oh, um, do you know what kind it is?

10
00:01:57,970 --> 00:01:59,810
Can't you tell just by looking?

11
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:01,990
I thought you knew black magic.

12
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:06,870
You gotta at least mention exactly where it was cast on you and what type it is.

13
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:10,890
It's actually not one type of spell but two.

14
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:12,730
The first one is here.

15
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:14,490
And the other...

16
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:17,930
Uh-uh.

17
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:20,230
...is my whole body.

18
00:02:22,110 --> 00:02:24,510
Wait, does that mean she's a beast man?

19
00:02:24,510 --> 00:02:27,510
Uh-huh. I saw one of these a long time ago.

20
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:30,390
She's what's called an artificially made beast man.

21
00:02:30,390 --> 00:02:34,390
I heard they're made using black magic to mix human and beast souls.

22
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:39,270
All right, then. I'll do whatever I can.

23
00:02:39,270 --> 00:02:44,750
This text. Looks like it's written in the Eastern language.

24
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:46,570
What's the spell type?

25
00:02:46,990 --> 00:02:48,530
Are you really a magic user?

26
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:52,650
It's a curse that activates if the caster doesn't touch it within a set time.

27
00:02:52,890 --> 00:02:55,290
So was the one who cast this that Miseru lady?

28
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:56,870
How long until it activates?

29
00:02:57,430 --> 00:02:59,270
And what happens when the time is up?

30
00:02:59,510 --> 00:02:59,990
Dunno.

31
00:03:00,150 --> 00:03:02,010
So you might want to remove it quickly.

32
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:04,830
I mean, you don't want to die with me, do you?

33
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:07,690
I'll let you go if you dispel it.

34
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:13,310
I'm not familiar with the letters, but I think I can remove this.

35
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:14,710
Hey, kid over there!

36
00:03:14,870 --> 00:03:15,130
Huh?

37
00:03:15,370 --> 00:03:16,550
Bring me something to eat!

38
00:03:16,550 --> 00:03:30,190
Out of curiosity, when was the last time you ate?

39
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:33,670
If you eat like that without chewing, it'll get stuck in your throat.

40
00:03:34,050 --> 00:03:34,670
Shut up!

41
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:37,310
How about you let me fix you up a nice, warm meal?

42
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:38,670
Hey, didn't I say don't move?

43
00:03:39,570 --> 00:03:41,050
Don't underestimate me!

44
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:46,930
All I'm gonna do is whip up something warm for your belly.

45
00:03:47,190 --> 00:03:47,770
That's all.

46
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:51,710
If you try to make me eat monster parts, I'll kill you.

47
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:53,110
I understand.

48
00:03:54,610 --> 00:03:55,050
Hmm.

49
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:59,850
If I'm remembering right, we picked up some mushrooms near the dryads.

50
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:00,590
Hmm?

51
00:04:01,090 --> 00:04:01,890
Hold on.

52
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:03,690
Are those little feet it sprouted?

53
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:06,270
Probably my imagination.

54
00:04:07,770 --> 00:04:09,690
Place a pod inside the magic circle.

55
00:04:09,690 --> 00:04:15,250
Toss some butter in to melt it, fry a few garlic cloves, and then add rice.

56
00:04:16,050 --> 00:04:17,670
Add in mushrooms and season it.

57
00:04:18,570 --> 00:04:20,990
Pour in water and let it simmer for a while.

58
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:26,390
Hmm.

59
00:04:27,410 --> 00:04:32,350
It feels shameful to be making something this simple compared to the dishes I had been making.

60
00:04:32,850 --> 00:04:37,270
But I hate the thought of letting a young'un go hungry, so I'll do whatever I've gotta do.

61
00:04:37,270 --> 00:04:40,170
Well, at the very least, I could put some cheese in.

62
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:42,390
It's ready.

63
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:46,430
I'll leave it here.

64
00:04:46,890 --> 00:04:48,270
Who'd even eat something like...

65
00:04:48,270 --> 00:05:02,230
This kid.

66
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:04,750
She has no table manners.

67
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:06,010
None!

68
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:08,510
Give me more, now!

69
00:05:08,830 --> 00:05:12,190
Do you think etiquette in the East is different from how we learn it here?

70
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:12,870
Doubt it.

71
00:05:13,130 --> 00:05:15,830
I've never once seen Shura eat as sloppy as she does.

72
00:05:16,390 --> 00:05:18,310
She was probably just raised poorly.

73
00:05:18,910 --> 00:05:20,170
Guess this is new for you.

74
00:05:20,170 --> 00:05:20,470
Huh?

75
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:36,530
What did you do that for?

76
00:05:36,710 --> 00:05:37,610
I hate mushrooms.

77
00:05:38,150 --> 00:05:38,810
She's picky.

78
00:05:39,290 --> 00:05:40,970
This has never happened before.

79
00:05:41,450 --> 00:05:41,970
Senshi.

80
00:05:44,270 --> 00:05:45,290
Your spoon.

81
00:05:45,890 --> 00:05:46,330
Huh?

82
00:05:46,330 --> 00:05:49,070
You're not holding it in your hand the right way.

83
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:49,550
Hey!

84
00:05:50,050 --> 00:05:51,910
Get any closer to me and you're dead meat!

85
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:56,890
Take that spoon, hold it properly, and pick up every piece of food you dropped on the floor.

86
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:58,210
What the hell?

87
00:05:58,490 --> 00:05:59,830
Hold on, me too!

88
00:06:00,150 --> 00:06:01,970
You shouldn't move while I'm dispelling!

89
00:06:02,330 --> 00:06:03,130
Ah!

90
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:09,050
Ah!

91
00:06:09,050 --> 00:06:09,210
Ah!

92
00:06:09,450 --> 00:06:09,730
Ah!

93
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:09,990
Ah!

94
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:13,890
Ah!

95
00:06:13,890 --> 00:06:17,430
This is how you hold the spoon.

96
00:06:18,030 --> 00:06:19,790
I can hold it how I want!

97
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:22,390
And this is the easiest way for me to do it!

98
00:06:22,570 --> 00:06:23,450
I'm sure it is.

99
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:27,170
Being forced to hold something in a way you're not used to must be vexing.

100
00:06:27,650 --> 00:06:28,270
But still...

101
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:29,550
Senshi, behind you!

102
00:06:29,550 --> 00:06:30,050
Ah!

103
00:06:32,790 --> 00:06:35,870
No effect.

104
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:38,010
Paper?

105
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:39,430
Senshi!

106
00:06:39,790 --> 00:06:40,370
Be careful!

107
00:06:40,370 --> 00:06:40,730
Ah!

108
00:06:43,890 --> 00:06:45,670
It's called a Tsujihiki knife.

109
00:06:45,970 --> 00:06:48,630
It's a type of carving knife used to finely slice meat.

110
00:06:49,350 --> 00:06:51,310
The length of the blade is long and sharp.

111
00:06:51,670 --> 00:06:54,330
While it may look intimidating, it's actually delicate.

112
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:59,030
Now, what do you think would happen if you swung it while gripping it like that?

113
00:06:59,530 --> 00:06:59,990
Senshi!

114
00:06:59,990 --> 00:07:15,710
As you can see, the tool's ability isn't used to its fullest, which can put you at a disadvantage.

115
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:24,510
Senshi!

116
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:25,730
Now, Laos!

117
00:07:25,730 --> 00:07:36,830
Catgirl, you're not hurt anywhere, are you?

118
00:07:37,830 --> 00:07:40,650
I probably startled you, and I'm sorry about that.

119
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:45,930
But there are reasons why there's good and bad ways to hold even the simplest of tools.

120
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,190
And I'd like you to keep that in mind.

121
00:07:48,530 --> 00:07:51,710
Also keep in mind you can't move while having something dispelled.

122
00:07:52,190 --> 00:07:54,690
If it were something worse, who knows what could have happened.

123
00:07:54,690 --> 00:07:58,950
Looks like your food already got cold.

124
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,830
Let me warm it up for you real quick.

125
00:08:03,410 --> 00:08:04,170
All right.

126
00:08:04,610 --> 00:08:06,630
So why were you even following us?

127
00:08:07,850 --> 00:08:12,730
This curse on my body, I've been looking for a way to remove it for a really long time.

128
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:21,030
I eventually figured out that the curse is tied to black magic, but wasn't able to find a magic user who specialized in it.

129
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:24,150
Not until we ran into that long year, anyway.

130
00:08:24,530 --> 00:08:25,130
Black...

131
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:27,190
Ancient magic has several types.

132
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:30,030
The one that I'm researching deals with drawing energy from a different...

133
00:08:30,030 --> 00:08:30,710
No excuses!

134
00:08:31,230 --> 00:08:32,730
I know you're capable of it!

135
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:35,610
I've seen living proof of your work, after all.

136
00:08:35,850 --> 00:08:38,850
You've combined a person and a monster with your black magic!

137
00:08:38,850 --> 00:08:45,570
And you guys are going deeper into the dungeon so you can remove the curse on that woman, aren't you?

138
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:48,910
In other words, that must mean you know of a way to get rid of it!

139
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:51,670
So then you should be able to break my curse too, right?

140
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:55,310
Remove this beast soul that possessed me so I can finally be free!

141
00:08:55,310 --> 00:09:01,930
I'm sorry, but that's just not something I can do for you.

142
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:03,290
Huh?

143
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:09,070
There are lots of things we still don't know about souls, but they're often compared to an egg.

144
00:09:10,330 --> 00:09:17,530
Usually, a soul is inside the body, or shell, but once the body breaks, the insides spill out and can't be put back together again.

145
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:22,970
A spell has been cast over this dungeon that creates a thick membrane on the inside of the shell.

146
00:09:22,970 --> 00:09:26,190
So, even if the soul gets damaged, it won't leave.

147
00:09:26,970 --> 00:09:32,250
In your and Fallon's cases, at the moment, there are two souls inside a single shell.

148
00:09:33,190 --> 00:09:37,930
Once two souls are mixed together, it's impossible to go back to how they were before.

149
00:09:38,850 --> 00:09:42,230
I already knew all that, but to put it so bluntly is harsh.

150
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:49,450
Wait, what? Then, why are you guys still continuing on such a dangerous journey?

151
00:09:49,450 --> 00:09:55,190
Well, for starters, I can't leave my sister in the state she's currently in.

152
00:09:55,750 --> 00:10:00,030
She might kill the next adventurer she runs into, or they might kill her.

153
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:02,410
We have to do something before then.

154
00:10:03,230 --> 00:10:07,490
Also, if we go back to the surface now, we'd get arrested for using black magic.

155
00:10:08,370 --> 00:10:11,150
Shiro probably will have reported this to the Island Lord.

156
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:16,710
So, you're saying I'm stuck like this forever?

157
00:10:17,210 --> 00:10:18,470
Hey, listen to me.

158
00:10:18,970 --> 00:10:22,630
This might be weird of me to say, but I'm really glad I ended up meeting you.

159
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:27,350
I have no idea what monster you're mixed with, but your speech and actions are perfectly human.

160
00:10:27,570 --> 00:10:29,370
Plus, you have no urge to murder anything.

161
00:10:29,370 --> 00:10:36,130
Looking at it a different way, if we manage to free Fallon, she could regain her original personality.

162
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:42,330
Just having learned that makes me feel, um, I'm really happy right now.

163
00:10:43,050 --> 00:10:43,530
Here.

164
00:10:43,710 --> 00:10:43,910
Huh?

165
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:49,430
This might be different from what you expected it to be, but maybe try Sina in a positive light.

166
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:51,210
Think of it as a new opportunity.

167
00:10:51,210 --> 00:10:57,110
The Lord of the Dungeon is far superior to me when it comes to the handling of ancient magic.

168
00:10:57,630 --> 00:11:02,150
If we try asking him, it's possible he'll teach us a thing or two about separating souls.

169
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:03,410
Hang on.

170
00:11:03,810 --> 00:11:05,770
Are you guys inviting me into your party?

171
00:11:06,370 --> 00:11:08,990
I mean, it'll be hard to return to the surface alone.

172
00:11:09,610 --> 00:11:11,570
I think I heard before that your name's Asabi.

173
00:11:12,470 --> 00:11:13,910
That was just an alias.

174
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:15,330
Then what's your...

175
00:11:15,330 --> 00:11:15,910
Izutsumi.

176
00:11:16,350 --> 00:11:18,010
My real name's Izutsumi.

177
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:19,470
And don't forget it.

178
00:11:21,210 --> 00:11:33,070
Laios, how long are you going to keep up this lifestyle?

179
00:11:34,030 --> 00:11:34,510
Father?

180
00:11:34,890 --> 00:11:36,930
You need to start living a proper life.

181
00:11:37,190 --> 00:11:40,530
I didn't allow you to leave home just for you to become a dragon slayer.

182
00:11:41,230 --> 00:11:42,490
Come back to the village.

183
00:11:43,010 --> 00:11:44,290
But Fallon is still...

184
00:11:44,290 --> 00:11:45,810
You can forget about that girl.

185
00:11:45,810 --> 00:11:46,170
Huh?

186
00:11:46,870 --> 00:11:50,370
Do you think someone like you could actually make it in the outside world?

187
00:11:50,370 --> 00:11:53,930
You couldn't fit in at school or the army and ran away.

188
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:57,450
You don't even have the skills to explore a dungeon either.

189
00:11:57,930 --> 00:12:02,610
Your party members are going to trick and rob you, just like the ones from your gold-stripping days.

190
00:12:02,870 --> 00:12:05,210
Because you're horrible at judging people's character.

191
00:12:06,110 --> 00:12:07,670
That was certainly true with me.

192
00:12:08,190 --> 00:12:12,670
You had considered me to be a good friend, but I'd always been uncomfortable being around you.

193
00:12:12,670 --> 00:12:13,890
You're so annoying!

194
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:15,210
We settled this already!

195
00:12:15,730 --> 00:12:17,730
Wait, come to think of it...

196
00:12:17,730 --> 00:12:19,430
Why are my parents even here?

197
00:12:19,890 --> 00:12:21,670
I haven't seen them in over ten years.

198
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:24,170
More importantly, where am I?

199
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:25,530
And what was I doing?

200
00:12:26,110 --> 00:12:27,270
Let's see here.

201
00:12:27,270 --> 00:12:33,090
I was getting kind of worried about Marcille.

202
00:12:33,590 --> 00:12:35,190
She'd been looking really tired.

203
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:40,090
Marcille, we'll take watch tonight, so you go get some rest.

204
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:41,030
Huh?

205
00:12:41,230 --> 00:12:42,170
How come?

206
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:43,470
You don't have to do that.

207
00:12:43,610 --> 00:12:44,770
Don't worry about it.

208
00:12:44,790 --> 00:12:45,410
It's fine.

209
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:46,510
What are you...

210
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:48,410
What's going on?

211
00:12:49,010 --> 00:12:51,110
I'm not even tired enough to sleep yet.

212
00:12:51,310 --> 00:12:51,810
All right?

213
00:12:51,870 --> 00:12:52,950
I'm getting up now.

214
00:12:52,950 --> 00:12:59,570
Before long, her peaceful sleeping breaths turned into unsettling groans.

215
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:01,790
Marcille, what's wrong?

216
00:13:01,830 --> 00:13:02,370
Are you okay?

217
00:13:02,690 --> 00:13:04,150
This looks pretty serious.

218
00:13:04,410 --> 00:13:05,270
Is it a monster?

219
00:13:05,690 --> 00:13:07,530
Yeah, a nightmare to be exact.

220
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:12,130
It possesses sleeping people, gives them bad dreams, and eats their emotions.

221
00:13:13,030 --> 00:13:16,290
At this rate, Marcille will keep getting weaker and eventually die.

222
00:13:16,910 --> 00:13:18,490
Rise and shine, Marcille!

223
00:13:18,570 --> 00:13:20,830
Don't force her awake or it'll damage her psyche.

224
00:13:20,830 --> 00:13:26,290
When Shiro got possessed that one time, Fallon went inside his dream and saved them.

225
00:13:27,190 --> 00:13:28,750
So, let's try out that method.

226
00:13:29,290 --> 00:13:29,950
Hang on.

227
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:31,190
You're gonna go into her dream?

228
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:34,130
Someone has to make her realize that she can wake up from it.

229
00:13:34,570 --> 00:13:37,830
You simply use the one who's dreaming as a pillow and...

230
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:46,070
I remember now.

231
00:13:46,310 --> 00:13:48,170
I was trying to save Marcille.

232
00:13:48,170 --> 00:13:51,110
But this is my dream.

233
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:53,830
Looks like the nightmare got a little taste of me.

234
00:13:54,150 --> 00:13:55,050
Well, that figures.

235
00:13:55,390 --> 00:13:57,870
Man, they really know what people hate, don't they?

236
00:13:58,250 --> 00:14:01,590
Although, since I've realized this is a dream...

237
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,970
My strongest servant, I summon thee!

238
00:14:07,710 --> 00:14:08,230
Huh.

239
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:11,890
Okay, now how do I go into Marcille's dream?

240
00:14:13,010 --> 00:14:15,770
She's right under my head at the moment, so...

241
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:18,550
That should mean I can dig down to get to her.

242
00:14:22,270 --> 00:14:24,090
This is why dreams are the best.

243
00:14:24,370 --> 00:14:25,850
Though it only works in your own.

244
00:14:25,850 --> 00:14:33,010
That was a close call.

245
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:35,370
I almost woke up from the feeling of falling.

246
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:37,410
Oh, wow.

247
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:39,810
This is Marcille's dream, huh?

248
00:14:40,890 --> 00:14:42,270
It's pretty amazing.

249
00:14:42,930 --> 00:14:43,890
Is someone there?

250
00:14:44,430 --> 00:14:45,950
What are you doing here?

251
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,770
This place is dangerous.

252
00:14:47,910 --> 00:14:48,830
You need to leave.

253
00:14:49,770 --> 00:14:51,350
Are you Marcille?

254
00:14:51,350 --> 00:14:53,490
Who are you?

255
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:54,910
It's me, Laios.

256
00:14:55,150 --> 00:14:57,330
The two of us are currently inside your dream.

257
00:14:58,030 --> 00:15:00,510
You should wake up so we can get out of this...

258
00:15:00,510 --> 00:15:02,050
What's that?

259
00:15:02,830 --> 00:15:04,130
Oh, no, it's coming.

260
00:15:04,590 --> 00:15:05,790
I have to run.

261
00:15:06,430 --> 00:15:07,190
What's coming?

262
00:15:07,410 --> 00:15:08,570
Hurry up, this way!

263
00:15:09,710 --> 00:15:11,070
It's swallowed them.

264
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:13,230
Papa and Pippi are gone now.

265
00:15:13,630 --> 00:15:14,670
Papa and Pippi?

266
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:17,390
A dream about being chased.

267
00:15:18,170 --> 00:15:20,190
It's a common dream, but still stressful.

268
00:15:20,190 --> 00:15:22,570
What was it Fallon said?

269
00:15:23,290 --> 00:15:25,830
Nightmares really love to feed on emotional wounds.

270
00:15:26,570 --> 00:15:28,490
They evoke stressful memories or trauma

271
00:15:28,490 --> 00:15:30,730
and display them as bad dreams.

272
00:15:31,110 --> 00:15:32,990
Then, they feed off the dreamer.

273
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:35,270
In order to prevent that,

274
00:15:35,350 --> 00:15:36,810
you need to protect those wounds.

275
00:15:38,910 --> 00:15:41,970
However, it's risky, so don't try it, okay?

276
00:15:42,530 --> 00:15:44,050
Alright, I got it.

277
00:15:44,450 --> 00:15:46,310
I'm gonna defeat that thing for you.

278
00:15:46,890 --> 00:15:47,910
You can't do that.

279
00:15:47,990 --> 00:15:48,730
It's dangerous.

280
00:15:48,730 --> 00:15:50,690
No need to worry about me.

281
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:52,950
I'm a lot stronger than I...

282
00:15:52,950 --> 00:16:06,190
What the hell is that thing?

283
00:16:06,330 --> 00:16:07,950
How am I supposed to know?

284
00:16:07,950 --> 00:16:10,330
So that's Marcelle's fear?

285
00:16:11,330 --> 00:16:13,170
It seems a little over the top,

286
00:16:13,370 --> 00:16:14,250
but even so,

287
00:16:14,330 --> 00:16:16,070
I don't think that I'll be able to defeat it.

288
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:18,950
She knew that this was a dream,

289
00:16:19,170 --> 00:16:20,610
that that thing wouldn't be a threat.

290
00:16:21,530 --> 00:16:22,930
I think we're safe now.

291
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:26,050
There's no such thing as safe here.

292
00:16:26,050 --> 00:16:28,550
No one can beat that monster.

293
00:16:30,010 --> 00:16:31,110
It'll be okay.

294
00:16:31,470 --> 00:16:33,310
We're gonna figure out how to defeat it.

295
00:16:34,050 --> 00:16:37,270
What is this thing that Marcelle fears?

296
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:39,090
It's definitely a monster.

297
00:16:39,890 --> 00:16:42,070
It has slow, crawly-like movements,

298
00:16:42,350 --> 00:16:43,110
several tentacles,

299
00:16:43,270 --> 00:16:44,390
and a hearty appetite.

300
00:16:45,150 --> 00:16:46,630
Not to mention it's gross.

301
00:16:47,450 --> 00:16:48,510
Maybe it's a bug?

302
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:51,710
Hmm, there aren't many bugs that large, though.

303
00:16:52,290 --> 00:16:53,450
What kind could it be?

304
00:16:53,970 --> 00:16:54,630
What kind?

305
00:16:55,350 --> 00:16:55,750
I know!

306
00:16:56,350 --> 00:16:57,190
It's a worm!

307
00:16:57,910 --> 00:16:59,710
Worms are a part of the dragon family.

308
00:17:00,110 --> 00:17:01,370
Their atrophied eyes and legs

309
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:02,510
make them caterpillar-like.

310
00:17:02,890 --> 00:17:03,750
If they're hungry,

311
00:17:03,950 --> 00:17:05,350
then they'll eat just about anything,

312
00:17:05,590 --> 00:17:06,930
and they're weak to fire and light.

313
00:17:07,490 --> 00:17:08,890
That's such a cool thing.

314
00:17:09,050 --> 00:17:09,950
Good job, me.

315
00:17:09,950 --> 00:17:14,790
I didn't even hear it.

316
00:17:15,490 --> 00:17:16,350
Watch out!

317
00:17:17,550 --> 00:17:18,970
We gotta run!

318
00:17:19,970 --> 00:17:22,430
That thing didn't touch you just now, did it?

319
00:17:22,730 --> 00:17:24,170
It was only a scratch.

320
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:24,810
Show me!

321
00:17:27,890 --> 00:17:29,590
What is this?

322
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:39,750
Crap.

323
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:41,370
She's even more scared.

324
00:17:41,910 --> 00:17:43,430
The nightmare's starting to get stronger.

325
00:17:48,170 --> 00:17:49,770
What vicious poison.

326
00:17:50,430 --> 00:17:52,870
What happens if I die in someone else's dream?

327
00:17:53,590 --> 00:17:54,150
No.

328
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:56,610
I'll fall right into its trap if I get anxious.

329
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:58,470
I've got to cheer her up.

330
00:17:59,230 --> 00:18:00,090
It'll be okay.

331
00:18:00,350 --> 00:18:02,090
You've got magic on your side.

332
00:18:02,470 --> 00:18:04,310
Defeating something like that'll be no problem.

333
00:18:06,130 --> 00:18:06,690
Magic.

334
00:18:06,690 --> 00:18:14,110
This place became even more unstable.

335
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:15,990
Did I say something bad?

336
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:17,110
I already...

337
00:18:17,110 --> 00:18:21,090
I already tried using some of my magic to defeat the monster,

338
00:18:21,710 --> 00:18:24,370
and that's how she ended up looking like this.

339
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:26,110
She?

340
00:18:26,590 --> 00:18:27,490
Wait a minute.

341
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:28,930
Is that doll Fallon?

342
00:18:28,930 --> 00:18:30,610
I get it now.

343
00:18:31,290 --> 00:18:34,330
Marcelle feels guilty about what her magic turned Fallon into.

344
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:36,750
Then defeating the monster must mean...

345
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:39,910
The thing Marcelle fears is death!

346
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:42,390
It's here again!

347
00:18:43,150 --> 00:18:45,150
You can't just run away all the time.

348
00:18:45,470 --> 00:18:47,290
You need to stand your ground and fight!

349
00:18:48,470 --> 00:18:49,310
Don't worry.

350
00:18:49,530 --> 00:18:51,390
There's nothing to be afraid of, Marcelle.

351
00:18:52,330 --> 00:18:54,870
If you die in this dungeon, you can get revived.

352
00:18:55,090 --> 00:18:55,730
Like Fallon.

353
00:18:55,870 --> 00:18:58,350
She's alive because you used revival magic on her.

354
00:18:58,590 --> 00:19:00,830
Besides, you're used to seeing corpses, right?

355
00:19:00,830 --> 00:19:07,870
Oh, no!

356
00:19:08,090 --> 00:19:08,850
It's sucking me in!

357
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:12,230
Wait, why is it only trying to pull me in?

358
00:19:12,330 --> 00:19:13,430
Grab my hand!

359
00:19:13,430 --> 00:19:18,190
It's not poison.

360
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:20,770
I'm aging at an incredibly fast rate.

361
00:19:21,470 --> 00:19:23,850
Hey, hold on a second, Marcelle.

362
00:19:24,130 --> 00:19:25,430
I can't breathe.

363
00:19:26,050 --> 00:19:27,130
Something's weird here.

364
00:19:27,690 --> 00:19:29,710
Is there a living creature that can do this?

365
00:19:30,390 --> 00:19:31,930
Maybe it's not a living thing at all.

366
00:19:32,690 --> 00:19:35,110
Does this mean you're gonna end up leaving me too?

367
00:19:35,610 --> 00:19:36,110
No.

368
00:19:36,450 --> 00:19:38,390
I'll be able to run again after I rest.

369
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:39,110
Liar!

370
00:19:39,690 --> 00:19:41,630
Everybody gives up on running with me!

371
00:19:41,630 --> 00:19:43,350
Then that thing swallows them!

372
00:19:43,990 --> 00:19:47,290
Papa, Pippi, Fallon, and everyone else too!

373
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:50,130
That's why I worked so hard to study lots of magic!

374
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:54,010
But if learning and using that magic made Fallon go away,

375
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:56,450
then what was it all for?

376
00:19:57,590 --> 00:20:00,770
If I could maybe ask, did your father die at a young age?

377
00:20:01,170 --> 00:20:04,070
We were at Papa's funeral, and Mama said

378
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:08,030
that when I run, I go a lot faster than everyone else.

379
00:20:08,230 --> 00:20:12,590
So that means I'm gonna have to say goodbye to a whole bunch of people.

380
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:14,450
You keep mentioning Pippi.

381
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:15,590
Who is that?

382
00:20:15,710 --> 00:20:16,290
My bird.

383
00:20:16,930 --> 00:20:17,850
I see.

384
00:20:18,690 --> 00:20:21,270
So it's not that Marcelle is afraid of death.

385
00:20:21,770 --> 00:20:25,090
She's actually worried her loved ones will die before she does.

386
00:20:25,090 --> 00:20:33,170
You need to calm down, Marcelle.

387
00:20:33,350 --> 00:20:35,890
The more scared you become, the stronger it gets.

388
00:20:36,310 --> 00:20:37,710
What am I supposed to do?

389
00:20:37,710 --> 00:20:38,830
I can't fight it!

390
00:20:38,930 --> 00:20:39,890
I can't do anything!

391
00:20:40,370 --> 00:20:41,330
No, you can!

392
00:20:41,630 --> 00:20:43,690
Because you're Marcelle, and you're amazing!

393
00:20:44,470 --> 00:20:46,250
I mean, these books say it all.

394
00:20:46,930 --> 00:20:49,370
I didn't see anything like this while in my dream.

395
00:20:50,030 --> 00:20:52,250
You've been working hard for a long time, right?

396
00:20:52,650 --> 00:20:53,490
Don't get discouraged!

397
00:20:53,890 --> 00:20:55,070
Have confidence in yourself!

398
00:20:55,650 --> 00:20:57,110
Marcelle, stay strong!

399
00:20:57,450 --> 00:20:57,850
No!

400
00:20:58,210 --> 00:20:59,070
That's enough!

401
00:20:59,070 --> 00:21:00,290
Let's just run!

402
00:21:00,410 --> 00:21:01,490
Please, stand up!

403
00:21:02,110 --> 00:21:04,310
How can I be strong when my magic's incomplete?

404
00:21:05,090 --> 00:21:10,450
If only I had that book you was carrying with him, I'd finally be able to complete my magic!

405
00:21:10,650 --> 00:21:12,230
Then go ahead and wish for that!

406
00:21:12,790 --> 00:21:15,470
If you wish hard enough for it, you can do anything!

407
00:21:15,690 --> 00:21:16,790
So don't be afraid!

408
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:18,870
You'll do it better the next time you try!

409
00:21:19,090 --> 00:21:20,370
Don't give up, Marcelle!

410
00:21:20,930 --> 00:21:21,570
Don't go!

411
00:21:21,730 --> 00:21:22,370
You can't!

412
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:23,410
Please, no!

413
00:21:23,410 --> 00:21:24,010
No!

414
00:21:33,610 --> 00:21:34,210
Yeah!

415
00:21:34,390 --> 00:21:35,230
That's the spirit!

416
00:21:35,570 --> 00:21:35,870
Go!

417
00:21:46,590 --> 00:21:47,670
Wait a minute.

418
00:21:47,850 --> 00:21:49,990
Is that even how you're supposed to use that?

419
00:21:49,990 --> 00:21:55,090
Oh, you're finally awake.

420
00:21:55,590 --> 00:21:57,290
You were both groaning in your sleep.

421
00:21:57,450 --> 00:21:58,110
Are you okay?

422
00:21:58,570 --> 00:22:00,430
I really don't remember what happened.

423
00:22:01,030 --> 00:22:03,610
I think I dreamt about being tired or something.

424
00:22:07,830 --> 00:22:09,270
Just going back to sleep!

425
00:22:09,390 --> 00:22:10,150
No, please!

426
00:22:10,230 --> 00:22:11,230
You have to stay awake!

427
00:22:12,390 --> 00:22:13,450
My dream?

428
00:22:14,070 --> 00:22:18,350
I can't remember it, but from what I can tell, it was probably a fun one.

429
00:22:18,350 --> 00:22:20,090
Looks like my plan actually worked.

430
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:21,310
Did something happen?

431
00:22:21,910 --> 00:22:23,110
Pass your pillow to me.

432
00:22:23,630 --> 00:22:24,010
Hmm?

433
00:22:27,430 --> 00:22:28,230
What's that?

434
00:22:28,410 --> 00:22:29,490
This thing is a nightmare.

435
00:22:30,210 --> 00:22:33,590
It sneaks inside of people's pillows and gives them bad dreams.

436
00:22:34,250 --> 00:22:35,850
But there sure are a lot of them.

437
00:22:36,590 --> 00:22:38,550
They must have been hiding in your pillow for a while.

438
00:22:39,070 --> 00:22:39,510
Seriously?

439
00:22:40,010 --> 00:22:41,590
Senshi, do you think we can eat these?

440
00:22:41,810 --> 00:22:43,770
I've been curious about what they taste like.

441
00:22:43,870 --> 00:22:44,950
Yeah, of course we can.

442
00:22:44,950 --> 00:22:47,870
First, make it spit out any dirt.

443
00:22:49,330 --> 00:22:51,710
By soaking them in some hot water like this.

444
00:22:52,570 --> 00:22:52,810
Huh?

445
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:55,790
Another name that the nightmare goes by is Shen.

446
00:22:56,070 --> 00:22:57,650
It's part of the dragon family.

447
00:22:57,990 --> 00:23:00,010
They kind of look like dragons, don't you think?

448
00:23:00,090 --> 00:23:01,230
You're joking, right?

449
00:23:01,650 --> 00:23:06,170
After melting some butter, place the nightmares in the pan and pour a bit of wine over top.

450
00:23:06,490 --> 00:23:07,290
Then cover.

451
00:23:07,290 --> 00:23:13,950
To finish the dish, add a touch of soy sauce.

452
00:23:14,610 --> 00:23:15,730
And it's ready.

453
00:23:18,210 --> 00:23:19,050
What's this?

454
00:23:20,050 --> 00:23:21,550
That's me when I was little.

455
00:23:21,810 --> 00:23:24,570
The dream that the nightmares ate turned into a mirage.

456
00:23:24,990 --> 00:23:27,510
I think I'm starting to remember things.

457
00:23:27,770 --> 00:23:28,590
Yeah, that's right.

458
00:23:28,790 --> 00:23:32,190
I was running away from something and suddenly a fluffy dog appeared.

459
00:23:32,190 --> 00:23:36,510
The dog and I went on an adventure to search for treasure together.

460
00:23:37,550 --> 00:23:39,250
It was a really fun dream.

461
00:23:39,390 --> 00:23:41,050
That's a pretty dirty looking dog.

462
00:23:41,270 --> 00:23:42,710
It doesn't look all that smart.

463
00:23:43,250 --> 00:23:44,390
What's wrong, Laios?

464
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:48,230
The way I remember it, it was a silver wolf and not a dog.

465
00:23:48,950 --> 00:23:49,330
Oh well.

466
00:23:49,910 --> 00:23:53,130
If I was able to help make her dream fun, then I'm glad.

467
00:23:53,130 --> 00:23:58,090
Oh, yeah.

468
00:24:02,490 --> 00:24:04,390
Oh, yeah.

469
00:24:04,390 --> 00:24:05,010
Oh, yeah.

470
00:24:05,010 --> 00:24:05,810
Yeah.

471
00:24:05,830 --> 00:24:17,870
Oh, yeah.

472
00:24:17,870 --> 00:24:18,210
Oh, yeah.

473
00:24:18,210 --> 00:24:22,270
Oh, yeah.

474
00:24:22,330 --> 00:24:22,650
Oh, yeah.

